From 266063cad24c094b3ce367726a93434df13f0076 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SpicyEggSalad <177426835+SpicyEggSalad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:41:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dsound: a song stopped by the pause menu goes on from where
 it was

The title's pause menu releases the song stream and builds a new one from the
start of the file, and a radio station builds one for another song. The host now
remembers what a stream had taken when the pause menu stopped it. The same song
again skips the packets already played; another song after the pause menu's own
music is replaced by the stopped one, whose packets are kept, then read on from
the wave bank (the kernel notes which file and byte each big read came from, and
the bank's entry table gives the song's end). A stream let go of on its last
packet plays that packet out instead of being cut. The stream log lines carry a
fingerprint of each packet and the stream's own state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/kernel/files.cpp |  30 +++++
 runtime/xdk/dsound.cpp   | 234 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 261 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

